column12:
        --- Retrieved from: https://www.polyu.edu.hk/eee/study/information-for-current-students/programme-documents/ ---

        --- Programme booklet: Master of Science in Electrical Engineering | MSc in EE: ['2.2 Programme Aims'] ---

- (a) To strengthen the professional knowledge of electrical engineers involved in engineering activities in the power  utilities, electricity utilization industries, railway systems, government organizations and consultancy companies;
- (b) To  provide  in-depth  study  of  the  state-of-the-art  developments  in  specialist  areas  of electrical  engineering: power  systems  engineering;  industrial utilization  and  power electronics;  railway  system;  energy  sources  and  planning;  control  and  automation;  and optoelectronics;
- (c) To develop an understanding of the integration between advanced technologies (such as computer  technology  and  communications)  and  the  traditional  branches  of  electrical engineering; and
- (d) To provide an opportunity for supplementing the core areas of electrical engineering study with topics in management, information science and related engineering fields.

column9:
        --- Retrieved from: https://www.polyu.edu.hk/eee/study/information-for-current-students/programme-documents/ ---

        --- Programme booklet: BEng/BSc (Hons) Scheme in Information and Artificial Intelligence Engineering | BEng/BSc (Hons) in IAIE: [] ---

(iv) a full academic record, giving subjects taken and grades attained, and the Grade Point Average (GPA)  for all  subjects  (this  shall  include  any  practical  training  undertaken, which fulfill the training credit requirement of the programme concerned);

